<title>USA: First Western sets 3-for-2 stock split.</title>
<headline>First Western sets 3-for-2 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>NEW CASTLE, Pa 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Western Bancorp Inc said Tuesday that its board declared a three-for-two stock split in the form of a 50 percent stock dividend to be distributed August 15 to shareholders of record July 28.</p>
<p>The company said fractional shares would be paid in cash based on the average of the five days' high and low trading prices through the record date, adjusted for the stock split.</p>
<p>Earlier Tuesday the company announced second quarter earnings of $0.64, up from $0.54 in the year-ago quarter. It also announced an increased quarterly cash dividend of $0.22 per share.</p>
